[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a reason why <code>ReaderT.run_read</code> is about <code>ReaderT.read</code> rather than <code>MonadReader.read</code>?</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ReaderT.run_read#doc\">docs#ReaderT.run_read</a></p>",
        "id": 602910965,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1781385547
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>there's no <code>MonadReader.run</code></p>",
        "id": 602912055,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1781385966
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well I think the question is about why the theorem states:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run_read</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monad</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ReaderT</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">read</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReaderT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>instead of</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run_read</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monad</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">read</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReaderT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 602912273,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1781386041
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes that's what I meant. For example <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=StateT.run_get#doc\">docs#StateT.run_get</a> is a statement about <code>StateT.run MonadState.get s</code> and this seems to be the general pattern.</p>",
        "id": 602912489,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1781386127
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Tracing this back to its source doesn't really provide an explanation: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ReaderT.run_read#doc\">docs#ReaderT.run_read</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=StateT.run_get#doc\">docs#StateT.run_get</a> were introduced within 3 hours by <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/commit/ae48feeb0729dd53b26345d695cb98568552771f\">feat: add <code>LawfulMonad</code> for <code>ReaderT</code></a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/commit/d0574d8eb1cdac06f3f73e4fd63a6552da850fcf\">feat: add <code>LawfulMonad</code> for <code>StateT</code></a> by Leo and have not changed since. My guess is that this is just a simple mistake.</p>",
        "id": 602914613,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1781386919
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or should it be stated for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=readThe#doc\">docs#readThe</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MonadReaderOf.read#doc\">docs#MonadReaderOf.read</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 602925945,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781391036
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have the same question but I don't see any corresponding <code>StateT.run_getThe</code>, should that exist?</p>",
        "id": 602926140,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1781391102
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Relatedly, I'm not sure why we have a <code>MonadReaderOf</code> instance for <code>ReaderT</code> but not a <code>MonadReader</code> instance</p>",
        "id": 602926270,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781391157
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would guess this is deliberate, but it would be great to see an explanation of why</p>",
        "id": 602926319,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781391179
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe that's because of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=instMonadReaderOfMonadReaderOf#doc\">docs#instMonadReaderOfMonadReaderOf</a></p>",
        "id": 602926376,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1781391200
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, I guess my question is whether that is supposed to be the only instance of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MonadReader#doc\">docs#MonadReader</a></p>",
        "id": 602960430,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781402969
    }
]